LNG:________blp_034_leve{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - BLP-034 levels diagnostic complete: gap map generated in docs/diagnostico-niveles.hcortex.md. Identified gaps fed BLPs 035-040 which correct all discrepancies between theory (v3.0) and practice.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________blp_038_cohe{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - BLP-038 coherence analysis revealed 4 critical issues: (1) AC-01 ambiguous about replacing vs adding learning channel, (2) LNG sigil collision between behavioral and contextual needed explicit differentiation, (3) elevate() API assumed features not yet in CODEC-CORTEX, (4) T-038.1 claimed new integration when learning.py already uses CODEC-CORTEX. Fix: renamed to elevate_behavioral(), added coexistence note, clarified three-line architecture.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________blp_041{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - BLP-041: metadata must be an ARQX:artifact entry in $1 (not $0.1 due to E033), declared in pipe-table. CODEC-CORTEX is not modified. The legacy '# section-0 METADATA' block is replaced but must have fallback during migration. 19/21 .cortex migrated. 2 legacy files (agents.cortex, CYCLE-00/cycle.cortex) are not CORTEX format — out of scope, degrade to level 0 with W001.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________blp_042{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - BLP-042: correct adoption sequence for CODEC-CORTEX as exclusive writer: (1) skill first, (2) handlers after, (3) migration backup(.bck)->rewrite at the end with feedback loop to skill. No version pinning — evolutionary compatibility.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

