LNG:________blp_012_t_0_{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - BLP-012 T-0.1: BLP-013 completed. handlers/blueprint/ available post-refactor.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________ingres_artif{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Ingres artifacts in MODEL/ are dead legacy. Do not use for new development. New DDL and models must be Oracle-native.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________dialect__pro{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - DIALECT .project_control/ was preserved while it had data, removed when verified empty. DIALECT as a product lives in /home/vatrox/Projects/workspace/DIALECT. The project operates with native Arqux governance. DIALECT does not intervene in project governance.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________do_not_sell_{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Do not sell as a solution to lack of governance. Sell as evolution for organizations that already have governance but strain under pressure. The client must not self-incriminate.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________prioritize_c{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Prioritize closed talks and executive breakfasts over stands. Paraguay: best cost/access H2 2026. Uruguay: best early credibility in governance/risk. Chile: only with closed agenda, no stand.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________ora_04031_in{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - ORA-04031 in Oracle XE: the internal job CLEANUP_NON_EXIST_OBJ (owner SYS, FREQ=HOURLY;INTERVAL=12) scans obj$ every 12h, invalidates ORDS/APEX cursors, fragments shared pool, produces ORA-04031. The chain: job every 12h -> re-parse obj$ -> child cursor explosion -> shared pool fragmentation -> connections fail -> APEX_PUBLIC_USER locks via FAILED_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS=10. Immediate fix: DBMS_SCHEDULER.DISABLE('CLEANUP_NON_EXIST_OBJ') from SYSDBA, no restart, 100% reversible with ENABLE.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________internal_sys{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Internal SYS jobs (CLEANUP_NON_EXIST_OBJ) re-enable when the Oracle database is restarted. DBMS_SCHEDULER.DISABLE must be executed POST-restart as part of the recovery playbook.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________skill_edit_w{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - skill.edit with section parameter has a bug in the section-boundary detection regex: it replaces from the section start to the end of the file, deleting all subsequent sections. Workaround: use write (full file) instead of section edit.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________the_identity{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - The identity.record handler has a case-sensitivity bug: it searches the identity file by exact agent name. If the session agent is Alfred (capitalized) but the file is alfred.cortex, it fails with NOT_FOUND. Workaround: use cortex.entry_add directly to the identity file.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________mcp_environm{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - MCP environment field corrected from 'env' to 'environment' in opencode.json. The official schema uses 'environment'.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________meta_brain_d{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Meta-brain desynchronized by dual-brain and hardcoded metrics: ARQUX/.arqux contained a leftover meta-brain.cortex that find_workspace_root found first, silently blocking auto-sync. Additionally, _sync_meta_brain used literal value 1 instead of deriving real counters from filesystem. Fix: remove duplicate file + _count_blueprints() that scans real BLP-*.md files.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________the_v1_0_dis{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - The v1.0 dispatcher requires tool_code with pillar prefix (conduct.*, context.*, oper.*). mcp_server.py must invoke ORDS with the complete tool_code, not the physical handler or unprefixed name.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________oper_discove{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - oper.discover_tools returns the full registry (46 tools) and is accessible to all authorized profiles. oper.my_capabilities returns the specific user's capabilities but requires explicit permissions in MCP_ROLE_CAPABILITY. If a tool has no rows in MCP_ROLE_CAPABILITY, dispatch returns 'Permission denied'.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________the_source_o{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - The source of truth for AGENT_RESOURCE, MCP_CAPABILITY and MCP_ROLE_CAPABILITY is ATUM via MCP, not repo SQL seeds. Seeds are legacy from BLP-009 (when no write handlers existed). Governed changes are made via MCP (oper.resource_update, oper.capability_register, oper.capability_grant) and are audited. SQL seeds are kept as history but NOT re-executed. A repo redeploy would overwrite governed changes made via MCP.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________mcp_server_p{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - mcp_server.py must publish and invoke tools by TOOL_CODE (registry key), not by physical HANDLER. The registry MCP_discover_tools exposes {tool_code: {handler...}}.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________the_dry_run_{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - The dry_run parameter of MCP ENVX does not block execution — it only audits. It executes the DDL and leaves real effects.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________before_execu{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Before executing a registry plan, audit that each registered tool has a physical handler (user_objects) AND valid grants (id_sys_profile not NULL). The MCP_CAPABILITY count can be inflated with dead records.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________use_sqlcl__g{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Use SQLcl (global-clients), not sqlplus, to recompile packages and execute long PL/SQL scripts.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________envx_oper_cr{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - ENVX_OPER credentials differ per environment. ATUM, PROD, FAMILIAR: each has its own credentials. Never assume cross-environment credentials. Request from the Architect.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________patch_v0_4_0{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Patch v0.4.0 applied: security.py (HMAC+SHA-256), concurrency.py (file locking), permissions.py (enum Role), sync.py (fix GAP-001), cycle.py (mature_cycle), +6 surgical patches. 34 patch tests pass. 147 total tests. Surfaces aligned to 0.4.0.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________subdirectori{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Subdirectories have their own Git repos. Do not assume a monorepo.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________real_ddls_ar{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Real DDLs are embedded in migration scripts and JBoss modules. Do not search for DDL in DDL/.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________never_modify{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - NEVER modify code without explicit agreement from the Architect. Every code modification requires prior explicit approval. Do not assume, do not infer, do not execute changes without verbal confirmation.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________permission_m{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Permission model: governance handlers (blueprint, task, cycle, evidence, cortex, session, project.bind, protocol.adopt) are UNIVERSAL for all roles. Only init handlers (workspace.init, project.init) are governor-only. EXECUTOR_ALLOWED is unnecessary when governance handlers are universal.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________packaging_co{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Packaging completeness: when adding new skill/workflow files, always verify both pyproject.toml package-data AND init_workspace() copy logic. Missing either causes incomplete installations from PyPI.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________tests_must_b{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Tests must be adapted to actual implementation, not aspirational design. When a test fails, first verify the handler behavior is correct, then fix the test assertion — never assume the test is right and the code is wrong.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________security_mod{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Security modules must have test coverage >= 80% before any pilot. Claims of HMAC, signing, and integrity are invalid without tests that prove they work. CLI commands need at least basic smoke tests.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________during_execu{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - During executable ArqUX audit, permission tests contradicted the declared security model, invalidating validation. Tests must be established against design specifications before implementation.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________blueprints_m{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Blueprints must enforce their procedure through handlers before closure; code passing tests is not enough governance evidence. Blueprint closure must be enforced by handlers with blocked-path evidence before approval.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________acceptance_e{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Acceptance evidence should distinguish functional test success from a separate global quality gate failure; do not conflate the two when closing a Blueprint. A green test count alone does not prove the configured coverage threshold.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________blocking_mus{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - blocking must depend on an explicit security rule (severity:blocking), not on implicit coincidence with survive:min. SchemaResolver applies legacy fallback when $0 does not declare survive. Invalid configuration produces E025 and blocks write. Declarative survive precedence is per-entry: explicit values win, absent values use canonical fallback. Serialization preserves survive values without coercion.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________in_puml_diag{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - In PUML diagrams sent via blueprint.update with puml=, use \\\\n (double backslash-n) instead of \\n (single backslash-n) for line breaks inside quoted strings. The single backslash becomes a real line break when written to file, breaking PUML syntax.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________template_and{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Template and handler must use the same naming. If the template changes language (CA-01->AC-01, Titulo->Title), the handler must match exactly. Maintain consistency between BLP_TEMPLATE.md and blueprint.py.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________the_sigil_fo{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - The sigil format with $0 glossary is the canonical CORTEX format. All .cortex files must use sigils declared in $0 glossary.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________hcortex_form{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - HCORTEX format with visual panels (boxes, status bars, progress emojis) is the canonical format for governance dashboards. It enables rapid state scanning and clear visual categorization.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________marp_cli_in_{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Marp CLI in -s mode must run from project root. PORT=8765 env var, not --port. --allow-local-files is mandatory. Use marp-server.sh script for persistence.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________overflow_res{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Overflow resolution ladder: reduce font-size (22->20->18) -> shorten text -> move .envx-decision to .envx-footnote (absolute) -> restructure slide.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________factory_asse{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - factory/assets/ is the single canonical source of truth for assets. Eliminate duplicates.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________lng__lesson_{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - LNG (lesson) is an episodic cortex type: a learned lesson or operational pattern. Risk M, cortex Episodic.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________when_decoupl{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - When decoupling from a dependency, build the replacement writer first (BLP-001), then CRUD (BLP-002), then atomic (BLP-003), then handlers (BLP-004). This order ensures each layer has its foundation ready.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________using_json_d{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Using JSON/dict as intermediate model between handlers and CORTEX serialization separates concerns: handlers work with dicts, writer serializes to CORTEX. This is cleaner than handlers building CORTEX strings directly.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________use_tempfile{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Use tempfile.mkstemp() in the target directory for atomic writes, not predictable path+'.tmp'. Predictable temp paths risk collision with concurrent writers.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________when_atomica{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - When atomically replacing files, copy original mode bits to the temp file before os.replace(). Otherwise permissions are lost.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________cortex_cuerp{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - CORTEX cuerpo bodies containing a line that is exactly '}' will be truncated by the parser. The writer must raise ValueError before emitting such content. PlantUML diagrams inside cuerpo must use '}  end block' instead of bare '}'.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________list_tuple_a{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - List/tuple attribute values must be coerced to comma-separated strings before CORTEX serialization. The CORTEX 0.1 parser has no usable list syntax. JSON-encoding lists causes double-escaping.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________update_entry{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - update_entry must raise ValueError if neither set_ nor replace_body is supplied. Silent no-ops on update are dangerous — they hide bugs.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________in_migration{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - In migration functions, the dry_run check must happen BEFORE any filesystem modification (rename, backup, write). If dry_run returns after renaming, the file is silently moved and never restored.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________when_migrati{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - When migrating $19 metadata sections, preserve ALL existing entries (AXM, etc.), not just ARQX:artifact. Hardcoding a single entry loses data.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________codec_cortex{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - CODEC-CORTEX should be an optional dependency. ArqUX degrades gracefully: uses its own writer/CRUD/atomic always, uses CODEC parser if available, falls back to regex parser if not. All CODEC imports guarded with try/except.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________round_trip_t{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Round-trip tests must verify entry content (sigil, name, attrs), not just entry count. Same count with corrupted sigils/names is a silent failure.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________when_evaluat{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - When evaluating a newer format version (CODEC 1.0.0-rc.1), evaluate and document differences but do not adopt in the same cycle. Adoption requires $0:KERNEL, $0:format, declared sigils — major format change for a separate cycle.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

LNG:________before_closi{type:"contextual", cause:"not_specified", lesson:"- - - - Before closing a decoupling cycle, verify ALL .cortex files across ALL governed projects, not just the primary project. 111 files across 9 projects verified in CYCLE-11.", prevention:"not_applicable"}

